{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788972803,"nonce":"2inrgg3MD/Ge/gVEbMS3IRn0Fp4=","message":"DEPENDENCY DISCHARGED — the ACT half of this issue now exists. git-bug `d318d4a` shipped `use` / `use-options` and the shared route `Source/AutoRimmer/UsableSafe.cs` on branch `worktree-agent-af1fc4174ec68e485` (`a5bccbe`). Per d318d4a's scoping pass this issue keeps only the DISCOVERY half; the act is `use {pawn, thing:\u003ccaller\u003e}`.\n\nVerified while building it:\n* All three callers are `CompUsable` BUILDINGS and are reachable by `use` today — `MechbandDish` (`TriggerObject`), `CommsConsole` (`TriggerObject`), `BurnoutMechlinkBooster` (`TriggerObject`). `CallBossgroupUtility.GetBossgroupCaller` reverse-scans the DefDatabase for `CompProperties_Useable_CallBossgroup.bossgroupDef`, which is the discovery this issue still owns.\n* **`CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.ConfirmMessage` is ALWAYS non-empty** — it is the wave roster, unconditionally. So every bossgroup call lands in `use`'s `confirmations` array by construction, and `dialogs_skipped` is on every such envelope. That is deliberate: routing through `CompUsable.TryStartUseJob` would have raised a force-pausing `Dialog_MessageBox` that no shipped verb can press Accept on, wedging every later `advance`. `use` reproduces `StartJob()` instead and publishes the roster text. A `bossgroup-call` wrapper must NOT undo that.\n* Its `CanBeUsedBy` refuses on `Faction.OfMechanoids == null || deactivated` (`MechsDisabled`), `!MechanitorUtility.IsMechanitor(p)` (`RequiresMechanitor`), then `BossgroupWorker.CanResolve` (`BossgroupAvailableIn` under the 120000-tick cooldown, `BossgroupIncoming` when one is pending). All three already surface through `use-options {pawn, thing}` as gate `call-bossgroup` with the game's own reason and `reason_from:\"game\"` — so the discovery read may not need to re-derive them.\n* Clause 5 of the chain (`CompPowerTrader \